3. HANDLER IS GENUINELY READ-ONLY — PASS (the scope question)
================================================================
Grepped ONLY added lines of the two non-test sources for every write primitive
(os.Remove, os.Rename, os.WriteFile, os.Create, os.MkdirAll, OpenFile, io.Copy,
os.Truncate, os.Chmod, os.Chtimes):

    --- internal/config/config.go (added lines) ---
    (no write-path calls added)
    --- internal/handlers/explorer/handlers.go (added lines) ---
    (no write-path calls added)

The repo-wide grep does hit os.WriteFile/os.MkdirAll nine times, but every hit is
in handlers_test.go / config_test.go building fixtures (e.g. handlers_test.go:319
`os.MkdirAll(sub, 0755)` creating the subdirectory whose exclusion is under test).
Test fixtures are not runtime writes.

I also checked the indirect write path, which a diff-only read would miss:
config.Load() ends in cfg.ensureDirectories(), so if ImportDirectory had been
added to that list, P14 would silently create directories. It was not:

    func (c *Config) ensureDirectories() {
        dirs := []string{ c.DataDirectory, c.UploadsDirectory, c.SettingsDirectory }
        ...os.MkdirAll(dir, 0755)...
    }

ImportDirectory is absent. The only `ensureDirectories` token in the config diff
is the unchanged context line. scanImportDirectory touches the import dir with
os.Stat and os.Lstat only. Nothing in P14 creates, modifies, or deletes a file at
runtime. P15's deletion logic has not arrived early.

