4. NO SECOND CSV PARSER — PASS
================================================================
Grep of added handler lines for encoding/csv, csv.NewReader, bufio, time.Parse,
ReadDir, WalkDir, filepath.Walk: "(none — no second parser, no manual traversal)".

handlers.go:475 builds a throwaway loader and delegates:
    importLoader := dataloader.New(importDir, store)
    infos, err := importLoader.GetFileInfo()
and copies fi.MinDate / fi.MaxDate straight through. Read
internal/services/dataloader/loader.go:677 GetFileInfo -> it calls
dl.scanCSVMetadata(file) (loader.go:730) for the range. So the dates come from
the existing loader path exactly as required; no parsing was reimplemented.

Non-recursion is structural, not conventional: GetFileInfo's inclusion rule is
`filepath.Glob(filepath.Join(dl.CSVDirectory, "*.csv"))` — a single-level glob.
A subdirectory cannot be reached and a non-.csv name cannot match.

================================================================
5. SYMLINKS NOT LISTED — PASS (read from code, plus an empirical control)
================================================================
Read the code rather than the test name. handlers.go:493:

    for _, fi := range infos {
        if li, err := os.Lstat(fi.Path); err == nil && li.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0 {
            continue
        }

The load-bearing detail is that this only works if fi.Path is the *unresolved*
glob path. Verified at loader.go:714 — GetFileInfo sets `Path: file`, where
`file` is the raw filepath.Glob result, never filepath.EvalSymlinks'd. So Lstat
inspects the link itself and the entry is dropped. Correct.

The test could have been vacuous: TestHandleImportScan_ExcludesNonCSVSubdirSymlink
sets `hasSymlink = false` and silently continues if os.Symlink fails, and its
`len(...) != 1` assertion would then hold trivially. I checked whether that
degradation was active on this machine:

    ln -s $T/real.csv $T/link.csv  ->  SYMLINK CREATION: OK
    lrwxrwxrwx ... link.csv -> /tmp/tmp.ptNFh8vFIh/real.csv

Symlinks work here, so link.csv really was created and really was excluded. The
assertion was genuinely exercised.

NOTED, non-blocking: "not listed" holds, but "not followed" is only true of the
result set. GetFileInfo calls scanCSVMetadata -> store.ReadFile(filePath) on the
symlink *before* the Lstat filter runs, so a symlinked file's contents are read
once and then discarded. Nothing leaks to the user and nothing is written, so
this does not violate the acceptance criterion, but a symlink pointing at a FIFO
or a very large file would stall or waste a scan. The code comment at
handlers.go:427-432 discloses this ordering honestly. Worth tightening in P15,
which will act on these paths for real.

Also fail-open: if os.Lstat errors, the `err == nil` guard skips the `continue`
and the entry is kept. Immaterial here (Glob just returned the path and os.Stat
already succeeded), but flagged for completeness.

